      "title": "[P1] Preserve compatibility capability on metadata-less results",
      "body": "When ChatGPT publishes the capability through `openai:set_globals` but the same result's standard `toolresult` has data and omits `_meta`, `capability` is `undefined` and this assignment clears the retained token. Without host `toolInfo`, that token is the sole identity, so an in-flight restore is rejected and later view-state edits cannot be saved; preserve the existing capability for metadata-omitted deliveries.",
      "confidence_score": 0.98,
      "priority": 1,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/mcp-app-v8/packages/owletto/src/mcp-apps/_shared/host.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 525,
          "end": 526
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "title": "[P2] Reset state for explicitly capability-less results",
      "body": "When a reused ChatGPT iframe receives a new `toolOutput` whose `toolResponseMetadata` is present but lacks the snapshot key, the extractor returns `null`. Because this fingerprint boundary only handles `undefined`, differing output bypasses `resetCurrentResult()` and carries the previous card's pagination, disclosure state, and tool name into the new card; apply the fingerprint fallback whenever no valid string capability identifies the result.",
      "confidence_score": 0.97,
      "priority": 2,
      "code_location": {
        "absolute_file_path": "/Users/burakemre/Code/lobu/.claude/worktrees/mcp-app-v8/packages/owletto/src/mcp-apps/_shared/host.tsx",
        "line_range": {
          "start": 636,
          "end": 642
        }
      }
    }
  ],
  "overall_correctness": "patch is incorrect",
  "overall_explanation": "The new result-identity state machine mishandles both omitted and explicitly absent snapshot capability metadata. These paths can either prevent restoration and persistence or leak view state between reused result cards.",
  "overall_confidence_score": 0.98
}

